[1.044461, "o", "i"]
[1.070777, "o", "t"]
[1.097247, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.736312, "o", "Initialized mnema project at ~/your-repository/.mnema\r\n  identity: mnid:c780206676aa22b7ea829f3beb6dcbe21d559ebe81d629df9acedfd90c9eed13\r\n"]
[1.736496, "o", "  backup key: created and enrolled — private half at ~/.mnema/identity/backup/078acd8998b877492678abe3a88f77a7a85ea8c7f7d78e7a2d74e72e80a14bc1.key\r\n"]
[1.736511, "o", "  Move that file off this machine: a backup left on this disk is lost with it.\r\n"]
[1.736581, "o", "\r\n  mnema writes no file of yours. In Claude Code the mnema plugin hands this record to\r\n"]
[1.736621, "o", "  each session on its own. Without it, `mnema brief > MNEMA.md` puts what governs this\r\n"]
[1.736637, "o", "  project in a file of its own — the `>` replaces the whole of the file it names — and\r\n"]
[1.736685, "o", "  one line in a `CLAUDE.md` brings that file in (an `AGENTS.md` is read there only\r\n"]
[1.73676, "o", "  where no `CLAUDE.md` exists):\r\n"]
[1.736777, "o", "    @MNEMA.md\r\n"]
[1.736901, "o", "\r\n  Commit `.mnema/` with the repository: the record travels with it, and every clone reads it.\r\n"]
[1.736918, "o", "  Next: `mnema decision record <title> <rationale>`; `mnema status` shows where things stand.\r\n"]
[3.351181, "o", "\u001b[2m# write down a call, with the reasoning and what was turned down\u001b[0m\r\n"]
