[21.851046, "o", "public: local integrity verified (T1/T2/T4); 1 tail(s); all events are signature-covered; 1 \r\nbackup key(s), which sign nothing until restored (see census — informational, not a break); \r\nexternal witness (T3): not covered — nothing outside this machine attests this record\r\n  census [backup-key] public \r\n078acd8998b877492678abe3a88f77a7a85ea8c7f7d78e7a2d74e72e80a14bc1: the backup key of \r\nmnid:c780206676aa22b7ea829f3beb6dcbe21d559ebe81d629df9acedfd90c9eed13, as the record declares \r\nit — a backup signs nothing until it is restored, so it has no tail (if it was restored and \r\nhas signed, that tail is not here)\r\nprivate: no record here — nothing has been written to this tree on this machine, so there \r\nis nothing to rule on\r\n"]
